 "figures": {
  "b1": {
   "title": "The floor in B1, through time",
   "caption": "Each line is a mean over stretches of 50 iterations: Experiment 37's two worlds with the floor (orange and violet), beside the 26 worlds of plain B1 that lived to 3,000 (grey: the median line, the middle half darker, nine in ten paler). Top left: the agents. Top right: the tokens a child starts with, all the tokens given to children over all the births (a logarithmic scale). Bottom left: births in an iteration per hundred agents. Bottom right: the share of its tokens a parent gives its child.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** Experiment 37's two runs (`python3 gol_lab.py run E37`): B1 at 10,000 tokens with a child never poorer than the median holding of its parent's neighbours (`B1-10000-60e522-s001`, `-s002`), to 3,000 iterations; beside the 26 of Experiment 2's 30 worlds of plain B1 (`B1-10000-s001` \u2026 `-s030`) that lived to 3,000.\n\n**Data.** From each run's `stats.jsonl`.\n\n1. Agents: the agents after each iteration's game.\n2. What a child starts with: the tokens given to children in a stretch (each birth phase's `reproTokenShare` times the tokens) over its births.\n3. Births: each birth phase's births over the agents it began with, times 100.\n4. What a parent gives: each birth phase's `meanInvestedShare`, the mean over its births of the tokens given over the tokens the parent held.\n5. Means over the stretches 0 to 49, 50 to 99, and so on; the band over plain B1's 26 worlds stretch by stretch.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py floorplain`."
  }
